# System-wide hostbased-auth trust list (companion to sshd_config.d/00-hostauth.conf).
#
# *** MANUAL OVERLAY — the real file is NOT committed. ***
# It lists the Vulcan login nodes whose users may SSH to this Aleph control-plane node via
# hostbased authentication (the login node vouches for the user; its host key must appear in
# /etc/ssh/ssh_known_hosts). This is how the aleph-tyk-pam PAM hook on a login node reaches
# tyk-admin.sh here to auto-provision every user's Tyk API key at login.
#
# At bake time, drop the REAL file (one trusted login-node IP per line) from the local
# manual-overlays/secrets dir over this dummy. The live real version lives on each control-plane
# node at /etc/ssh/shosts.equiv — copy it from a running node if you need the current set.
#
# Format — one IP (or hostname) per line:
# <login-node-1-ip>
# <login-node-2-ip>
# <login-node-3-ip>
